# The subfield of `p`-th powers of the function field of an elliptic curve

This file collects the vocabulary used by `Work.MotV.derivZeroPow`:

* `PthPow K p` is the subfield `{z : K | ∃ w, w ^ p = z}` of a field `K` of exponential
  characteristic `p`, realised as the range of the Frobenius map;
* `deriv_eq_zero_of_mem_PthPow`: a derivation kills `p`-th powers;
* `KpAdjoin E p γ` is the subfield `N(E)^p(γ)` of `N(E)` generated by the `p`-th powers and `γ`;
* `eq_top_of_mem_genX_genY`: a subfield of `N(E)` containing the constants, `genX` and `genY`
  is everything (every element of `N(E)` is a quotient of polynomial expressions in `x`, `y`);
* `algebraMap_mem_PthPow`: over an algebraically closed field every constant is a `p`-th power.
-/

